-- title:
--   Level automorphisms act on the supersingular charts (q=2)
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ with $q = 2$, a nonzero modulus $M'$ not divisible by $q$, and a prime $\ell$ with $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell \mid M'$. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $q$ a nonunit of $A$, let $W$ be a finite set of places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A)\,M'$ over $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ whose members are exactly the supersingular places (rational, affine geometric, with supersingular value of the geometric $j$), let $\mathrm{hle}$ witness $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M' \le \mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$, and let $R_0$ be a constant reduction of the base-changed full modular function field whose residue field is that function field over $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$, compatible with coefficientwise reduction of Laurent series. Further data: an index $\zeta$ of a primitive $q$-th root of unity; valuation subrings $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ indexed by the projective line over $\mathbb{Z}/q$ and $O_{\mathrm{SS}}$ indexed by $W$, subject to the hypotheses (summarised here) that $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ at the line at infinity is the ring of quotients of Laurent series over $A$ with nonzero reduced denominator, that the $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ are injectively indexed, obtained from the one at infinity by pullback along $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma$ for suitable $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, and permuted by all such pullbacks; and that each $O_{\mathrm{SS}}\,s$ cuts out $A$ on constants, is compatible with $R_0$ and with the place $s$, is fixed by every pullback along $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta'\,\gamma$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, and contains an element all of whose translates by elements of $A$ are units. Finally let $\mathcal{C}$ be a $\mathrm{SemistableCovering}\,q\,M'\,A\,W$, let $R_{\mathrm{SS}}\,s$ be regular prolongations onto $\mathcal{C}.\mathrm{FSS}\,s$ with integer rings $O_{\mathrm{SS}}\,s$, agreeing with the charts $\mathcal{C}.\mathrm{CSS}\,s$ in integers and residues, and let $\mathrm{discS}$, $\mathrm{coordS}$ be a disc family for $R_{\mathrm{SS}}\,s$ off the nodes of $\mathcal{C}.\mathrm{CSS}\,s$, subject to: transport of discs by semilinear automorphisms fixing $A$, its maximal ideal and the image of $jq$, under which the non-node places correspond; the chart domain is the union of the discs at non-nodes; the place map sends each such disc to its centre and is constant off the domain; and the node set and the discs are equivariant for the residue automorphisms induced by the subgroup generated by the $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$. The conclusion quantifies over a further index $\zeta : \mathrm{Idx}\,q$ (shadowing the earlier one), over $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and over $s \in W$: writing $g$ for the semilinear automorphism of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ with trivial base part attached to $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma^{-1}$, there is an automorphism $\varphi$ of $\mathcal{C}.\mathrm{FSS}\,s$ over $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ such that $g$ preserves the integer ring of the chart $\mathcal{C}.\mathrm{CSS}\,s$ in both directions and its residue map intertwines $g$ with $\varphi$, and such that $(\mathcal{C}.\mathrm{CSS}\,s).\mathrm{placeMap}(g \cdot P) = \varphi \cdot (\mathcal{C}.\mathrm{CSS}\,s).\mathrm{placeMap}\,P$ for every place $P$ in the chart's domain.
--
--   This is the naturality clause for the supersingular charts in the assembly of a semistable covering of the full-level modular curve at $q = 2$, with the auxiliary prime $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ dividing $M'$: the level automorphisms attached to $\Gamma_0(M')$ act on each supersingular chart through an automorphism of its reduced function field, compatibly with the chart's place map. It is used in the existence theorem for such coverings together with the corresponding clauses for the Igusa components.
